### Generating QR codes with different error correction levels

The `qrcode` library allows developers to generate QR codes with different levels of error correction. The error correction level determines the amount of data redundancy in the code, which enables the QR codes to be more resilient to damage or interference. QR codes can be generated with four error correction levels:

- `ERROR_CORRECT_L`: Low level error correction (7%)
- `ERROR_CORRECT_M`: Medium level error correction (15%)
- `ERROR_CORRECT_Q`: Quarte level error correction (25%)
- `ERROR_CORRECT_H`: High level error correction (30%)

Here is an example that generates a QR code with high level error correction:

``` python
import qrcode

# Generate QR code with high level error correction
qr = qrcode.QRCode(version=1, error_correction=qrcode.constants.ERROR_CORRECT_H, box_size=10, border=4)
qr.add_data("https://www.example.com")
qr.make(fit=True)
img = qr.make_image(fill_color="black", back_color="white")

# Save the final QR code image
img.save("qr_high_error_correction.png")
```

### Generating QR codes with different data types

The `qrcode` library can generate QR codes that encode different types of data, such as URLs, email addresses, phone numbers, and more. Simply pass the data to the QR code generator, and the library will automatically format it correctly based on the data type.

Here is an example that generates a QR code with an email address:

``` python
import qrcode

# Generate QR code with email address
qr = qrcode.QRCode(version=1, box_size=10, border=4)
qr.add_data("mailto:foo@example.com")
qr.make(fit=True)
img = qr.make_image(fill_color="black", back_color="white")

# Save the final QR code image
img.save("qr_email_address.png")
```

Similar to the email address, you can generate QR codes with phone numbers, SMS messages, Wi-Fi access points, vCards, and many other data types. In every case, the `qrcode` library handles the data formatting and encodes it properly in the QR code.
